:name: STM32F4 usart_irq dynamic test
:description: Loads the usart_irq firmware under test and bridges USART2 to a TCP socket for byte-level echo verification.

# Run this with:
#   renode --disable-gui -P 4567 usart_irq_test.resc &
# Then, from another terminal:
#   python3 echo_test.py
#
# -P 4567 puts Renode's own monitor console on a TCP port instead of an
# interactive prompt attached to this shell's stdin - without it, Renode
# exits immediately when run in the background (no terminal to read from).
# --disable-gui skips the GUI entirely, which this headless test doesn't need.

using sysbus
mach create "usart_irq_test"

# stm32f4_discovery.repl ships with Renode itself (Antmicro's official
# platform description for the real ST STM32F4-Discovery board). It defines
# a genuine, non-stub USART2 peripheral wired to the NVIC, and real GPIO
# port models - unlike QEMU's equivalent, whose GPIOD is an
# "unimplemented-device" stub (see recon/PLATFORM.md for how that was found).
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/stm32f4_discovery.repl

# Absolute path to the actual compiled firmware under test. Re-seed a defect,
# rebuild (see setup.sh's printed rebuild command), and this same script
# picks up the new .elf automatically on the next Renode run - no edit needed
# here unless the firmware moves to a different path.
$elf?=@/Users/gowthamreddys/Desktop/hydron-evaluation/stm32-pilot/firmware/libopencm3-examples/examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/usart_irq/usart_irq.elf

sysbus LoadELF $elf

# Exposes USART2's serial traffic as a plain TCP socket on port 3456. Once
# this is running, anything that can open a TCP connection (this pilot uses
# echo_test.py) can send/receive bytes exactly as if it had a real serial
# cable connected to the chip's UART pins.
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal 3456 "uart_bridge" false
connector Connect sysbus.usart2 uart_bridge

# Actually starts CPU execution - without this, the ELF is loaded but the
# emulated core never runs, and nothing would ever respond on the socket.
start
